    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2M815H3kzG4g6aP6hfeqVJy)_\n\n## What\nTyping a partial name in `C-x b` and pressing `RET` created a new buffer. Vertico's default `vertico-preselect` is `prompt`, which keeps the typed text selected, so `RET` submits it. `sp-completion` now sets `vertico-preselect` to `first`, so the best match is selected.\n\n- `M-RET` (`vertico-exit-input`) still submits exactly what you typed, for a new buffer name.\n- The setting applies to every Vertico prompt, not only buffers. If you want it for buffers only, say so and I will scope it.\n- Updated the literate doc `sp-completion.org` and CHANGELOG.org.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). Please restart, then try `C-x b` with a partial name and `RET`, and `C-x b` with a new name and `M-RET`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBUXbpjoYMcDSiH1vN)_",
